    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n68292" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοιχ-ᾰλίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>
		(also acc. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοιχαλίν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Ho.</u>
					3.1
				</span></i>
			), ἡ, 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοιχάς</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Rom.</u>
				7.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				8.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
				8(1).264
			</span></i>, etc.; in religious sense, <i>unfaithful to God,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ep.Jac.
				4.4
			</span></i>: so as Adj., <i>adulterous</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενεά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
					12.39
				</span></i>
			, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μοιχεία</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>2 Ep.Pet.</u>
				2.14
			</span></i>.</div>
